//! [P1.1 PR 4] Pre-baked periodic column polynomial coefficients for DEEP-ALI.
//!
//! Each circuit's transition constraint involves periodic columns (Poseidon
//! round constants + round-active flags) that are public, deterministic
//! functions of the trace row. To check the DEEP-ALI identity
//! `Q(z) * Z_D(z) == C(T(z), T(gz), z)` at the OOD point z, the verifier must
//! evaluate each periodic column at z. These polynomials are the inverse NTTs
//! of the periodic column values over the trace domain, baked in at compile
//! time so the on-chain program doesn't re-derive them per call.
//!
//! Values are verified against the off-chain prover's `inverse_ntt` output by
//! the `circuit_0_periodic_coeffs_match_verifier_constants` test in
//! `stark/src/compact.rs` — that test MUST pass whenever this file changes.

// ============================================================================
// Circuit 0 (subscriber_ownership): trace_length = 32, 4 periodic columns.
// rc0/rc1/rc2: Poseidon t=3 round constants (per-row, rows 0..29 active),
// flag: 1 for rows 0..29, 0 for padding rows 30..31.
// ============================================================================

